{"parentUuid":"d56feb9f-2a86-4e56-b16c-4d558a54d401","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"d37afbb0-360b-4567-8521-559960af01b1","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012BPe7qXMVn2XXjsKgrLYg9","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Zero-connection assistant use-cases — PROVEN e2e on Haiku (Jul 19, #34840+)\n2\t\n3\tElia's product direction: a personal assistant that gives real administrative value **without connecting to any system** (no OAuth, non-invasive). Target audience = his sister's clients (small-business owners + consultants) whose pain is administrative, not technical. Keep it simple, NOT complex automations. Live-tested end-to-end on **pilot-12d5ec (claude-haiku-4-5)** — the cheapest tier handled all of it flawlessly.\n4\t\n5\t## The mechanism = pre-filled links the user clicks. Agent never touches the account.\n6\t\n7\t### 1. Calendar READ — Google Calendar secret ICS feed\n8\t- User: Settings → click their calendar → \"Integrate calendar\" → \"Secret address in iCal format\" → copies the `.../calendar/ical/<email>/private-<hash>/basic.ics` URL, pastes to agent once.\n9\t- Agent fetches it anytime → sees all events in real time. **Read-only** (cannot write/create/invite via ICS). Never say \"full access\" — say \"I can see your whole calendar.\"\n10\t- Deep link to settings: `https://calendar.google.com/calendar/r/settings`\n11\t\n12\t### 2. Calendar WRITE — Google render TEMPLATE link (NOT an .ics file)\n13\t- `.ics` files open the desktop Calendar app, not Google Calendar. For a Google user, use the render link instead:\n14\t```\n15\thttps://calendar.google.com/calendar/render?action=TEMPLATE&text=TITLE&dates=START/END&add=guest@x.com&location=PLACE&details=BODY&sf=true&output=xml\n16\t```\n17\t- Opens Google Calendar in the browser with everything pre-filled; user taps Save. **Guests via `&add=email`** → when the user Saves, Google actually emails the invite. So this IS real \"send invite\" — no OAuth.\n18\t- `details=` = prep text embedded in the event body (agenda, talking points, attendee background). A real file **attachment** is NOT possible via link (needs Calendar API + Drive/OAuth); offer a Drive link in details instead.\n19\t- **Time format = the one recurring bug:** write times in **UTC with `Z`** (Israel IDT = UTC+3, so 12:00 local = `T090000Z`). Local-time-without-Z caused a real off-by-one error (wrote 10:45 for a requested 11:45). → this is the case for **self-verification before send** on the model.\n20\t\n21\t### 3. Email — Gmail compose link\n22\t```\n23\thttps://mail.google.com/mail/?view=cm&fs=1&to=RECIPIENT&su=SUBJECT&body=BODY\n24\t```\n25\t- Opens a Gmail compose window in the browser where the user is already logged in, subject+recipient+body pre-filled; user reviews and hits Send. Agent doesn't touch, read, or authenticate to the account. This is the answer to \"don't you need to connect to my email?\" → **No.**\n26\t\n27\t### 4. Meeting-summary flow (replaces the ChatGPT step + ties it to the calendar)\n28\t- User forwards the transcript (or audio) from their recording tool once (agent does NOT auto-connect to the recording software). Agent summarizes, pulls key points + action items, drafts follow-up, stores it, and links it to the calendar event so it resurfaces the prep before the next meeting.\n29\t\n30\t## Product framing for the sister/consultant audience\n31\t\"What the bot can do for you first: manage your calendar reminders without connecting to your calendar. You share context once, it runs the routine — preps you before meetings, reminds you after to log.\" Administrative glue, not automation. It can't *execute inside* systems, but it *manages* the routine and knows what's going on.\n32\t\n33\t## Honesty boundaries to keep (never fabricate)\n34\t- ICS = read-only. No file attachment on calendar events via link. No auto-connect to recording software. Never invent a connect URL (the c56df3 lesson). Ask for a real email instead of guessing a guest's address.\n35\t"}]},"uuid":"350fd422-61f3-442d-82da-1f20e9598315","timestamp":"2026-07-30T06:19:29.113Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/workspace/agent/zero_connection_assistant_usecases.md","content":"# Zero-connection assistant use-cases — PROVEN e2e on Haiku (Jul 19, #34840+)\n\nElia's product direction: a personal assistant that gives real administrative value **without connecting to any system** (no OAuth, non-invasive). Target audience = his sister's clients (small-business owners + consultants) whose pain is administrative, not technical. Keep it simple, NOT complex automations. Live-tested end-to-end on **pilot-12d5ec (claude-haiku-4-5)** — the cheapest tier handled all of it flawlessly.\n\n## The mechanism = pre-filled links the user clicks. Agent never touches the account.\n\n### 1. Calendar READ — Google Calendar secret ICS feed\n- User: Settings → click their calendar → \"Integrate calendar\" → \"Secret address in iCal format\" → copies the `.../calendar/ical/<email>/private-<hash>/basic.ics` URL, pastes to agent once.\n- Agent fetches it anytime → sees all events in real time. **Read-only** (cannot write/create/invite via ICS). Never say \"full access\" — say \"I can see your whole calendar.\"\n- Deep link to settings: `https://calendar.google.com/calendar/r/settings`\n\n### 2. Calendar WRITE — Google render TEMPLATE link (NOT an .ics file)\n- `.ics` files open the desktop Calendar app, not Google Calendar. For a Google user, use the render link instead:\n```\nhttps://calendar.google.com/calendar/render?action=TEMPLATE&text=TITLE&dates=START/END&add=guest@x.com&location=PLACE&details=BODY&sf=true&output=xml\n```\n- Opens Google Calendar in the browser with everything pre-filled; user taps Save. **Guests via `&add=email`** → when the user Saves, Google actually emails the invite. So this IS real \"send invite\" — no OAuth.\n- `details=` = prep text embedded in the event body (agenda, talking points, attendee background). A real file **attachment** is NOT possible via link (needs Calendar API + Drive/OAuth); offer a Drive link in details instead.\n- **Time format = the one recurring bug:** write times in **UTC with `Z`** (Israel IDT = UTC+3, so 12:00 local = `T090000Z`). Local-time-without-Z caused a real off-by-one error (wrote 10:45 for a requested 11:45). → this is the case for **self-verification before send** on the model.\n\n### 3. Email — Gmail compose link\n```\nhttps://mail.google.com/mail/?view=cm&fs=1&to=RECIPIENT&su=SUBJECT&body=BODY\n```\n- Opens a Gmail compose window in the browser where the user is already logged in, subject+recipient+body pre-filled; user reviews and hits Send. Agent doesn't touch, read, or authenticate to the account. This is the answer to \"don't you need to connect to my email?\" → **No.**\n\n### 4. Meeting-summary flow (replaces the ChatGPT step + ties it to the calendar)\n- User forwards the transcript (or audio) from their recording tool once (agent does NOT auto-connect to the recording software). Agent summarizes, pulls key points + action items, drafts follow-up, stores it, and links it to the calendar event so it resurfaces the prep before the next meeting.\n\n## Product framing for the sister/consultant audience\n\"What the bot can do for you first: manage your calendar reminders without connecting to your calendar. You share context once, it runs the routine — preps you before meetings, reminds you after to log.\" Administrative glue, not automation. It can't *execute inside* systems, but it *manages* the routine and knows what's going on.\n\n## Honesty boundaries to keep (never fabricate)\n- ICS = read-only. No file attachment on calendar events via link. No auto-connect to recording software. Never invent a connect URL (the c56df3 lesson). Ask for a real email instead of guessing a guest's address.\n","numLines":35,"startLine":1,"totalLines":35}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"d56feb9f-2a86-4e56-b16c-4d558a54d401","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts"